\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Conquering Prince and Lord of glory,
\par Majesty enthroned in light;
\par All the heavens are bowed before Thee,
\par Far beyond them spreads Thy might;
\par Shall not I fall at Thy feet,
\par And my heart with rapture beat;
\par Now Thy glory is displayed,
\par Thine ere yet the worlds were made?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. As I watch Thee far ascending
\par To the right hand of the throne,
\par See the host before Thee bending,
\par Praising Thee in sweetest tone;
\par Shall not I too at Thy feet
\par Here the angels' strain repeat,
\par And rejoice that heaven doth ring
\par With the triumph  of my King?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Power and Spirit are o'erflowing,
\par On me also be they poured;
\par Every hindrance overthrowing,
\par Make Thy foes Thy footstool, Lord!
\par Yea, let earth's remotest end
\par To Thy righteous sceptre bend,
\par Make Thy way before Thee plain,
\par O'er all hearts and spirits reign.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lo! Thy presence now is filling
\par All Thy church in every place;
\par Fill my heart too; make me willing
\par In this season of Thy grace;
\par Come, Thou King of Glory, come,
\par Deign to make my heart Thy home,
\par There abide and rule alone,
\par As upon Thy heavenly throne!
\par                                     Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

